      "name": "Grilled Chicken Breast with Corn and Zucchini Quinoa Bowl",
      "macros": {
        "protein_g": 51,
        "fat_g": 11,
        "carbs_g": 69
      },
      "prep_time": "15 minutes",
      "cook_time": "25 minutes",
      "ingredients": [
        "7.5 oz chicken breast per serving",
        "1.5 cups cooked quinoa per serving",
        "1 ear fresh corn, kernels cut off",
        "1 medium zucchini, diced small",
        "1 cup cherry tomatoes, halved",
        "1 tbsp olive oil (total for entire batch)",
        "Salt to taste",
        "1 tbsp lemon juice",
        "1 tsp garlic powder",
        "1 tsp dried parsley"
      ],
      "steps": [
        "Cook quinoa according to package directions, using 3 cups water for 1.5 cups dry quinoa. Set aside.",
        "Season chicken breasts with salt, garlic powder, and dried parsley.",
        "Heat a large non-stick skillet or grill pan over medium heat. Add 1 tbsp olive oil for the entire batch of 4 servings.",
        "Cook chicken breasts 6-7 minutes per side until internal temperature reaches 165°F. Rest 5 minutes then slice.",
        "In the same pan over medium heat with residual oil, add corn kernels and diced zucchini. Cook 5-6 minutes until tender and lightly golden.",
        "Add halved cherry tomatoes and cook 2 minutes more until softened.",
        "Stir cooked quinoa into the vegetable mixture. Add lemon juice and toss to combine.",
        "Serve sliced chicken over quinoa vegetable mixture.",
        "For toddlers: cut chicken into small soft pieces and ensure quinoa vegetables are soft enough."
